inZOI ground-truth intervention -- PASS, replicated on two runs

Unmark exactly one primitive's bRenderCustomDepth via the engine's own
setter, and require exactly that id's pixels to disappear from the mask.
This is the only check in the project that cannot be satisfied by
coherent-but-wrong data: every other one reads the buffer and asks whether
it looks like object ids; this one changes the world and requires the
buffer to follow.

  run 1  slot 102  InstancedStaticMeshComponent  161,787 px (15.8%) -> 0
         others 44,351 -> 46,370 px  (GREW 4.6%: the unmarked surface
         stopped occluding the geometry behind it)

  run 2  slot 1    StaticMeshComponent           696,837 px (68.1%) -> 0
         others 327,163 -> 326,971 px (flat, 0.1%: slot 1 is the sky
         sphere, which is behind everything, so removing it reveals
         nothing new)

Different objects, different magnitudes, both to exactly zero. Note the
'UNMARKED' line in each: it confirms the intervention ACTUALLY RAN. An
earlier version reported FAIL on a run where the selected slot was held by
no live marked primitive, so nothing was changed and there was nothing to
judge. See DEBUGGING.md 8.13-8.15.

